<title>USA: Sola International Inc Q2 net falls.</title>
<headline>Sola International Inc Q2 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited Statements of Income</p>
<p>		(Amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				  Second		  Second   Second</p>
<p>				    Qtr.		   Qtr.	Qtr.</p>
<p>				    1997		   1997	1996</p>
<p>						     as adjusted</p>
<p> Net sales		  $128,194		$128,194  $95,866</p>
<p> Net income		    6,969		  11,077    9,000</p>
<p> Net income per share	 0.27		    0.44     0.39</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>  of shares outstanding   25,460		  25,460   22,911</p>
<p>				   First		   First    First</p>
<p>				    Half		    Half     Half</p>
<p>				    1997		    1997,    1996</p>
<p>						     as adjusted</p>
<p> Net sales		 $237,730		 $237,730 $191,788</p>
<p> Net Income		   9,131		   19,996   15,443</p>
<p> Net income per share	0.37		     0.82     0.67</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>  of shares outstanding  24,351		   24,351   22,887</p>
<p>NOTE: 97 Q2 includes pro forma adjustment to cost of sales to remove the non-recurring charge of $6.5 million, or $7.2 million for the half year, amortization of a step-up of inventories to fair value arising from the AO acquisition.</p>
<p>SIx-month results include pro forma adjustment to eliminate in-process research &amp; development expense associated with the AO acquisition, as it is non-recurring.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
